On Thursday 18 December 2008 18:41, nzpierre@gmail.com wrote:

> Newbie question, but how do you stop the cockatrice from decomposing?
> I recall trying this and the cockatrice (maybe a chickatrice?) rotted
> away.

You don't. It's a perishable weapon. It's useful if you find a cockatrice 
nest to leave most of the inhabitants alive, especially if you have 
teleport control, so you can zip back and forth to get yourself a fresh 
corpse for a big zoo or a dangerous place like Orcus Town.

It won't decompose very quickly, though; I once petrified most of the Fort 
Ludios garrison (the ones who didn't kill each other with their wands of 
lightning) with one corpse, and Croesus had a convenient second cockatrice 
in his throne room.

